  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Multiplying matrices is at the heart of graphics, scientific computing and neural networks. For centuries it took n cubed multiplications. In 1969 Volker Strassen showed that a 2 by 2 block product needs only 7 multiplications, not 8, and so beat n cubed."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Strassen's matrix multiplication"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the seven stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The ordinary method, dividing into blocks, Strassen's seven products, and a worked example."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then the running time, how it is used in practice, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=6]"
      }
     ]
    }
